    "id": "news-1791483103422-7",
    "title": "Fuel prices in Somalia rise again, reaching up to $1.19 per liter",
    "original_title": "Qiimaha shidaalka Soomaaliya oo mar kale kor u kacaya",
    "slug": "fuel-prices-in-somalia-rise-again-reaching-up-to-1-19-per-liter",
    "summary": "Fuel prices in Somalia have increased over the past few days, with some traders selling a liter for $1.15 to $1.17, and up to $1.19 in certain areas. This marks a renewed surge in the market, up from around $1.10 per liter just days earlier.",
    "content": "Mogadishu, 8 October 2026 — Fuel prices in Somalia have risen again in recent days, with some traders selling a liter for between $1.15 and $1.17, while in certain parts of the country the price has reached $1.19 per liter. Just days ago, the price was around $1.10 per liter, indicating a renewed upward trend in the market over a short period.\n\nThe increase comes amid ongoing pressure on global fuel markets due to tensions in the Middle East and risks related to shipping and maritime routes. These international factors are contributing to volatility in local fuel prices, as Somalia relies heavily on imported fuel.\n\nFuel is a critical commodity for Somalia, affecting transportation, electricity generation, and the cost of goods. The recent price hike is likely to have a ripple effect on the cost of living, as businesses may pass on higher fuel costs to consumers.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, which sends significant remittances to family members in Somalia, the rising fuel prices could mean that remittances cover less than before. Many families rely on these funds for daily expenses, including fuel for cooking, lighting, and transportation. Additionally, diaspora-owned businesses in Somalia may face increased operational costs.\n\nThe price fluctuations also highlight the vulnerability of Somalia's economy to external shocks, given its dependence on imports. As global oil markets remain unstable, Somali consumers and businesses may continue to experience unpredictable fuel costs.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/10/08/qiimaha-shidaalka-soomaaliya-oo-mar-kale-kor-u-kacaya/",
    "source": "goobjoog.com",
    "source_name": "Goobjoog",
